  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> be the relation defined on the set of all real numbers such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ykPcJ",
      "text": "reflexive and symmetric but not transitive",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
